The TypeScript adaptation accepts only maps whose output layout equals the
input's default layout, refuses every map that changes the channel count or
layout, AMBI/USR/UNK/UNSD channel ids, signed or space-led indices, quoted
options and non-default input masks, and copies planes instead of reassigning
pointers so that a duplicated channel never aliases another output plane.
The original source and full notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
